Notebook[{Cell["Lepton-quark and lepton-gluon scattering with a different \
tagged parton, step 2 (FORM route): spin and colour algebra", "Title"], 
  Cell["Same task and same output format as the FeynCalc route, now with FORM \
doing the Dirac algebra.  Input: the amplitude records of step 1.  Output: \
Results/FORM/Algebra.wl.\n\nMathematica only writes the amplitudes to a file \
(amplitudes.inc, in the vocabulary described in form/common.h), runs the FORM \
programs in the form/ directory, and reads their output back.  Open those \
programs to follow the algebra: Born.frm, RealQG.frm, RealGQ.frm, \
PhotonQG.frm and PhotonGQ.frm square the amplitudes (conjugation, spin sums, \
density matrices, gamma traces, polarization and colour sums, kinematics).  \
Each program is run twice, with the preprocessor variable SPIN = U (spin \
average) and SPIN = P (helicity difference).", "Text"], 
  Cell["Load and export", "Section"], Cell["Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirecto\
ry[], \"..\", \"..\", \"FeynFacet\", \"FeynFacet.wl\"}]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["records = LoadAmplitudes[][\"Records\"];\nwork = \
ResultsDirectory[\"FORM\"];\nWriteFORMAmplitudes[<|\"Born1\" -> \
records[\"Born\"][[1]],\n  \"RealQG1\" -> records[\"RealQG\"][[1]], \
\"RealQG2\" -> records[\"RealQG\"][[2]], \"RealGQ1\" -> \
records[\"RealGQ\"][[1]], \"RealGQ2\" -> records[\"RealGQ\"][[2]],\n  \
\"PhotonQG1\" -> records[\"PhotonQG\"][[1]], \"PhotonQG2\" -> \
records[\"PhotonQG\"][[2]], \"PhotonGQ1\" -> records[\"PhotonGQ\"][[1]], \
\"PhotonGQ2\" -> records[\"PhotonGQ\"][[2]]|>, work]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Import[FileNameJoin[{work, \"amplitudes.inc\"}], \"Text\"]", 
   "Input"], Cell["Run the FORM programs", "Section"], 
  Cell["program[name_] := FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"form\", \
name}];\nDo[RunFORM[program[name], work, \"Define\" -> {\"SPIN=\" <> spin}], \
{name, {\"Born.frm\", \"RealQG.frm\", \"RealGQ.frm\", \"PhotonQG.frm\", \
\"PhotonGQ.frm\"}}, {spin, {\"U\", \"P\"}}];\nFileNames[\"*.m\", work]", 
   "Input"], Cell["Born.frm (SPIN=P) prints G5Check, the difference between \
the trace Tr[gamma^a gamma^b gamma^c gamma^d gamma5] computed with the \
explicit gamma5 and -4 i eps^{abcd}; it must vanish.", "Text"], 
  Cell["bornLog = Import[FileNameJoin[{work, \"Born-SPIN=P.log\"}], \
\"Text\"];\ng5Check = StringDelete[First[StringCases[bornLog, \"G5Check =\" \
~~ Shortest[x__] ~~ \";\" :> x]], Whitespace | \"(\" | \
\")\"];\nRequire[g5Check === \"0\", \"gamma5 normalization check failed in \
Born.frm\", g5Check];\n\"G5Check = \" <> g5Check", "Input"], 
  Cell["Read the results", "Section"], Cell["FORM writes its results in \
Mathematica syntax.  The squares are functions of D (through the symbol D of \
the declarations); the unpolarized results of the channels with an incoming \
gluon or photon still need the averages 1/(D-2) per vector boson (FORM does \
not divide by polynomials).", "Text"], Cell["born = <|\"Unpolarized\" -> \
ReadFORM[work, \"BornU.m\"], \"Polarized\" -> ReadFORM[work, \
\"BornP.m\"]|>;\nRequire[Simplify[(born[\"Unpolarized\"] - 2 ee^4 eq^2 ((s^2 \
+ u^2)/t^2 - (4 - D)/2)) /. u -> -s - t] === 0, \"Born square differs from \
the textbook result\"];\nRequire[Simplify[(born[\"Polarized\"] - 2 ee^4 eq^2 \
(s^2 - u^2)/t^2) /. u -> -s - t] === 0, \"Polarized Born square differs from \
the expected result\"];\nborn", "Input"], Cell["real = <|\"QG\" -> \
<|\"Unpolarized\" -> ReadFORM[work, \"RealQGU.m\"], \"Polarized\" -> \
ReadFORM[work, \"RealQGP.m\"]|>,\n  \"GQ\" -> <|\"Unpolarized\" -> \
ReadFORM[work, \"RealGQU.m\"]/(D - 2), \"Polarized\" -> ReadFORM[work, \
\"RealGQP.m\"]|>|>;\nphoton = <|\"QG\" -> <|\"Unpolarized\" -> ReadFORM[work, \
\"PhotonQGU.m\"]/(D - 2), \"Polarized\" -> ReadFORM[work, \
\"PhotonQGP.m\"]|>,\n  \"GQ\" -> <|\"Unpolarized\" -> ReadFORM[work, \
\"PhotonGQU.m\"]/(D - 2)^2, \"Polarized\" -> ReadFORM[work, \
\"PhotonGQP.m\"]|>|>;\nRequire[FreeQ[photon, den], \"A photon propagator was \
not recognized by the FORM programs\", Cases[photon, _den, \
Infinity]];\nFactor[real[\"GQ\"][\"Polarized\"] /. spe3 -> 0]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Save", "Section"], Cell["algebra = <|\"Born\" -> born, \"Real\" -> \
real, \"Photon\" -> photon|>;\nSaveResult[\"Algebra\", algebra, \
\"FORM\"];\nKeys[algebra]", "Input"]}, WindowSize -> {1000, 800}]
